---
description: Airside shared working rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` and `GAME.md` at the repo root before making changes — they are
the shared contract for every contributor and override anything else.

Key points:
- Unity game lives in `game/Airside/` (Unity 6.3 LTS).
- The git repo is the single source of truth. `git pull --rebase origin main`
  before work; keep commits narrow; update `GAME.md` and `CHANGELOG.md` in the
  same commit; push to `origin` straight after.
- One change, one owner. Use a `feature/<name>` branch or worktree for parallel
  work with non-overlapping files.
- Domain/Simulation code stays independent of Unity scenes. Injected clock,
  seeded random, reserve resources before use, frame rate must not change
  simulation outcomes, preserve save compatibility.
- Run `scripts/test-unity.sh` and confirm the project compiles before committing
  behaviour changes.
